#+TITLE: Hosted runtime tests share persistent Windows logging preferences
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug

* Evidence
MR !507 Windows job17673025002: 2453 checks passed, two cleanup failures.
PROTOCOL-PREPARED-CLOSE-RESTORES-BEFORE-LOOP-EXIT and
CAD-RESTORE-SESSION-IS-IDEMPOTENT-AND-CLOSES-CURRENT-LOG-FIRST
failed deleting Drawing1 logs with a Windows sharing violation. The hosted
child was waited for, but LOGFILEMODE and LOGFILEPATH are shared persisted
preferences: another concurrent process can reopen the same log.

* Correction under qualification
DRIVE-HOSTED-ENGINE gives each child CLAUTOLISP_REGISTRY_FILE in its own
workdir and restores the caller environment afterwards. No locked file
is ignored and no cleanup assertion is removed. Require both regressions
and the full native Windows ALFE suite to pass before closing this issue.

* Resolved in 2.3.91
The private registry store removes both locked-log failures on Windows.
MR !507 Windows job17673828857 passes2459/2459 with no skips.
MR !476 Windows job17673832295 has neither log failure; its independent
CLI/pathname spelling assertion was corrected and passes2/2 on Windows.
